  "section_notes": "The final text sets S2 at a 7% permanent failure-rate ceiling (above the 5% limit discussed, so Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10 passes), with per-model results given to purchasers of that model and to regulators but not published. S5 is no longer an automatic recall: exceeding 8 per 100,000 triggers notification, a risk assessment and regulator review, and recall occurs only if the regulator finds an unacceptable ongoing risk, which benefits Halcyon's 9.9-rate Ember 8. S3 delays the new-unit shut-off requirement to 24 months (beyond the 12-month acceptable range), while the 6-year retrofit deadline meets Northwind's red line."
